I just encountered this interesting situation which looks like
a major bug at first glance, but is probably just an annoyance.

I am in a shop, and I have picked up everything without paying.
Now, it just so happens that a rock mole has eatten away part of
the side of the shop, although there is still no easy way out of
the shop yet.  So I move to the rock mole opening and stand there.
This space is still considered "in" the shop so no alarm sounds
yet.  I drop all of my unpaid items here.  I type "Iu" to make
sure I have no unpaid items left.  I type "Ix" to make sure I have
no unpaid used up items.


	  ###
      ----@..--        ---------
      |.......|    ####.       |
      |.......|    #   |       |
      |......@-#####   |     > |
      ---------        ---------
	   shopkeeper


Everything looks dandy, until I step north one space.  Suddenly,
an alarm sounds and I am accused of stealing all of the unpaid items
I just dropped.

At first I thought this is a major bug.  Thinking about it more,
I can see why the game works this way.  The problem has to do with
where I dropped the unpaid items.  I presume that the shop code
treats a shop doorway as "in" the shop for purposes of the player
and his pack.  However it treats a shop doorway as "outside" the
shop for purposes of objects on the ground.  This is why you can
pick up an object that lies in a shop doorway and not be charged
for it -- because the object is not "in" the shop even though you are.

So assuming the above is true, what happened was that I moved to
a shop doorway (that the rock mole created) carrying unpaid items,
but no alarm sounds since I am still "in" the shop.
I then dropped the items, but because the items are now "outside"
the shop, they are not removed from unpaid status (even though
I no longer have them).

To fix this, I propose that "Ix" tell you of items not in your
pack that still have unpaid status, and that leaving the shop
now would not be looked at kindly.

This is probably a much easier fix than redefining the way shop
doorways work.

